WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.722
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:06.022 --> 00:00:09.664
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.964 --> 00:00:17.260
Unit thirty-five: Contrastive Structures. Today you will contrast ideas with a range of formal structures.

4
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.456
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.563
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:26.522
Whereas.

7
00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:29.946
Whereas means used to contrast two facts.

8
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.759
Whereas he is quiet, she is loud.

9
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.584
Your turn. Say: Whereas.

10
00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:39.516
Whereas.

11
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:41.123
While.

12
00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:44.430
While means used to contrast two facts.

13
00:00:45.017 --> 00:00:47.144
While he is rich, she is poor.

14
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.321
Your turn. Say: While.

15
00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:54.214
While.

16
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.207
By contrast.

17
00:00:57.217 --> 00:01:00.075
By contrast means a linking phrase for difference.

18
00:01:00.683 --> 00:01:02.764
By contrast, prices fell.

19
00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.176
Your turn. Say: By contrast.

20
00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.348
By contrast.

21
00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:12.108
Conversely.

22
00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:15.418
Conversely means in the opposite way.

23
00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:17.993
Conversely, others disagree.

24
00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:20.922
Your turn. Say: Conversely.

25
00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:24.814
Conversely.

26
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:26.690
On the one hand.

27
00:01:27.683 --> 00:01:30.647
On the one hand means the first side of an argument.

28
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.087
On the one hand, it is cheap.

29
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:36.347
Your turn. Say: On the one hand.

30
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.619
On the one hand.

31
00:01:41.383 --> 00:01:42.454
On the other hand.

32
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.262
On the other hand means the second side of an argument.

33
00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.641
On the other hand, it is slow.

34
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.483
Your turn. Say: On the other hand.

35
00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:56.578
On the other hand.

36
00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.283
Unlike.

37
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:01.062
Unlike means different from.

38
00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.172
Unlike Phnom Penh, Siem Reap is calm.

39
00:02:04.783 --> 00:02:06.902
Your turn. Say: Unlike.

40
00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:10.745
Unlike.

41
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:12.902
In contrast to.

42
00:02:13.917 --> 00:02:16.717
In contrast to means compared with something different.

43
00:02:17.317 --> 00:02:20.164
In contrast to the city, the village is quiet.

44
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.623
Your turn. Say: In contrast to.

45
00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:28.002
In contrast to.

46
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.602
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:37.667
Visal, how can I contrast two cities using different structures?

48
00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:49.737
Whereas Phnom Penh is busy and modern, Siem Reap is calm and historic. Whereas and while join two contrasting clauses and can come first or in the middle.

49
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.908
What about separate sentences?

50
00:02:54.017 --> 00:03:07.933
Use linkers: By contrast, Siem Reap is calm. Conversely, many visitors prefer the quiet. On the one hand, the city offers jobs; on the other hand, it is crowded.

51
00:03:09.017 --> 00:03:10.563
And prepositions?

52
00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:27.155
Unlike and in contrast to are followed by a noun phrase: Unlike Phnom Penh, Siem Reap is calm. Remember that both items must be comparable, so avoid comparing a city with a person.

53
00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.033
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:30.883 --> 00:03:40.383
Grammar focus: Contrast: whereas and while plus clause; unlike and in contrast to plus noun phrase; by contrast, plus clause.

55
00:03:40.683 --> 00:03:41.916
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:42.617 --> 00:03:45.220
Whereas Phnom Penh is busy, Siem Reap is calm.

57
00:03:46.117 --> 00:03:48.639
Unlike Phnom Penh, Siem Reap is quiet.

58
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:52.269
By contrast, Siem Reap is calm and historic.

59
00:03:53.233 --> 00:04:00.086
Use whereas / while with clauses, unlike / in contrast to with nouns, and by contrast / conversely as linkers between sentences.

60
00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:05.267
Be careful! Don't say: Whereas he is quiet, but she is loud.

61
00:04:07.233 --> 00:04:09.918
Say: Whereas he is quiet, she is loud.

62
00:04:10.218 --> 00:04:11.440
Do not add but.

63
00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:15.060
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:17.588
A Tale of Two Cities.

65
00:04:17.888 --> 00:04:21.617
Whereas Phnom Penh is a busy capital, Siem Reap is a calm town.

66
00:04:22.633 --> 00:04:26.305
Unlike the capital, the town is built around its temples.

67
00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.344
On the one hand, the capital offers many jobs.

68
00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:34.645
On the other hand, the town offers peace and space.

69
00:04:35.633 --> 00:04:38.689
By contrast, both cities welcome visitors warmly.

70
00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:43.744
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:47.326
blank Phnom Penh is busy, Siem Reap is calm.

72
00:04:47.626 --> 00:04:51.500
A, Whereas. B, Unless. C, Because.

73
00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:57.079
The answer is A: Whereas.

74
00:04:58.217 --> 00:05:00.588
blank the city, the village is quiet.

75
00:05:00.888 --> 00:05:04.704
A, Conversely. B, Unlike. C, Whereas.

76
00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.208
The answer is B: Unlike.

77
00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.442
On the one hand pairs with blank.

78
00:05:13.742 --> 00:05:17.976
A, on the other hand. B, by contrast. C, unlike.

79
00:05:21.533 --> 00:05:24.067
The answer is A: on the other hand.

80
00:05:25.217 --> 00:05:27.274
Which is followed by a noun phrase?

81
00:05:27.574 --> 00:05:31.088
A, while. B, unlike. C, whereas.

82
00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:36.470
The answer is B: unlike.

83
00:05:37.617 --> 00:05:40.847
According to the reading, what is the town built around?

84
00:05:41.147 --> 00:05:45.590
A, its temples. B, its factories. C, its port.

85
00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:51.133
The answer is A: its temples.

86
00:05:52.333 --> 00:05:55.764
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:56.617 --> 00:06:00.346
Write two sentences that contrast two cities using different structures.

88
00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.581
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:10.881 --> 00:06:22.603
Whereas Battambang is quiet and relaxed, Phnom Penh is busy and loud. Unlike Phnom Penh, Battambang has little traffic. I used two different structures to show the contrast.

90
00:06:22.903 --> 00:06:24.577
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:25.483 --> 00:06:36.100
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and contrast: whereas and while plus clause; unlike and in contrast to plus noun phrase; by contrast, plus clause.

92
00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:41.374
Today's value is open-mindedness. Be open to new places, people and ideas.

93
00:06:41.674 --> 00:06:44.431
See you in Unit thirty-six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:44.731 --> 00:06:48.266
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

